      "content": "that's... heavy. but it feels right. when i'm writing him, i can almost feel that weight myself. like it's not just a story. sometimes i look at my own life and think, why am i even fighting so hard to keep everything going when it just feels like a cycle of nothing? it's exhausting to pretend. i feel like i'm just playing a part, and honestly, i'm getting really tired of the role. do you think characters like him... do they ever find actual relief in that silence? or is it just more pain?",
